  "next_id": 88,
  "notes": [
    {
      "at": [
        -12,
        -34
      ],
      "id": 87,
      "text": "A 74HC595 shift register drives eight LEDs. The firmware shifts each byte out bit by bit on PA7 (data),\nPA5 (shift clock) and PA4 (latch), the pins of SPI1. MR goes to VDD and OE to GND, and the chip needs\nits supply on VCC and GND. Run (F5): a light runs across the LEDs, then they count in binary.\nAnalyzer > Logic shows the clock and data lanes of the board and the chip's outputs (U2.Q0...)."
    }
  ],
